68); and fully rough regime (hs+ > 68). In particular, in fully rough conditions, the height of the roughness elements definitely exceeds the laminar sublayer thickness and the friction factor f becomes independent of the Reynolds number and is only a function of the relative pipe roughness hs/D, where D is the pipe diameter. Nikuradse also pointed out that, regarding the velocity profile in terms of the nondimensional wall variables u+ = u/uτ and y+ = yuτ /ν where y is the distance from the wall, the logarithmic region still exists but is shifted by the quantity U +, as shown in Fig. 2. Near the wall, the viscous sublayer is highly perturbed by the presence of roughness and in the fully rough regime it is entirely
